WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.455
Welcome to Sponsored Brands.

00:00:01.455 --> 00:00:07.273
In this video, you'll learn how to create and manage effective advertising campaigns that help increase

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.091
your brand visibility on Amazon.

00:00:09.091 --> 00:00:14.909
Sponsored Brands are ads featuring your brand logo, a custom headline, a lifestyle image or video,

00:00:14.909 --> 00:00:16.000
and multiple products.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.091
These ads appear in prominent shopping placements, helping you increase visibility and direct shoppers

00:00:21.091 --> 00:00:24.364
to your Amazon Brand Store or product detail pages.

00:00:24.364 --> 00:00:28.000
They support brand discovery and consideration during the customer journey.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.037
Let's begin with Ad Placements.

00:00:30.037 --> 00:00:34.111
Sponsored Brands can appear in three key locations on Amazon.

00:00:34.111 --> 00:00:39.000
At the top of shopping results, where they immediately catch shopper attention.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.931
Within shopping results, mixed with organic listings to maintain visibility as shoppers scroll,

00:00:43.931 --> 00:00:50.000
and on product detail pages where they can influence decisions closer to the point of purchase.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Understanding where your ads appear helps you anticipate shopper behavior.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.136
To set up a Sponsored Brands campaign, go to the Amazon Ads console.

00:00:58.136 --> 00:01:01.000
Start by naming your campaign to keep things organized.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.500
Then, set your start date and assign a daily budget.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.000
This budget determines how often your ad appears each day.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.667
If your daily budget runs out, your ads will pause until the next day, potentially missing, valuable

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:14.000
traffic.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Keep in mind, budgets reset at midnight.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.818
Next, choose a campaign goal.

00:01:18.818 --> 00:01:21.000
There are two Sponsored Brands objectives.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Drive page visits, directs shoppers to specific product detail pages, or your Amazon Store.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
This helps increase engagement with your brand.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.714
Grow Brand Impression Share focuses on gaining visibility, especially at the top of shopping results

00:01:34.714 --> 00:01:37.000
to support brand recognition and reach.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.895
Choosing the right goal helps Amazon match your ad with the best settings, including format, targeting,

00:01:42.895 --> 00:01:44.000
and bid strategy.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Once you've chosen your goal, you can apply bid adjustments to support it.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.000
These adjustments help you prioritize certain placements or audiences.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:58.562
For example, increasing your bid for top of shopping results helps maximize visibility in premium

00:01:58.562 --> 00:01:59.000
positions.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:04.040
If you want to reach new audiences, boost your bid for new to brand shoppers, people who haven't

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.000
purchased from you in the past year.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.474
These options give you more control over how your budget is spent and can improve performance in

00:02:10.474 --> 00:02:11.000
key areas.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.727
Now, let's choose an ad format.

00:02:13.727 --> 00:02:16.000
Sponsored Brands offers three options.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Video ads play automatically in shopping results.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.000
They're great for showcasing product use or telling your brand story.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Product collection ads display up to three items side by side.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.000
This is ideal for featuring bestsellers or complementary products.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.158
Store Spotlight Ads highlight multiple store pages, allowing you to direct shoppers to different

00:02:35.158 --> 00:02:37.000
product categories within your brand.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.000
Each format is designed to align with specific campaign goals and shopper behaviors.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.000
To help your brand reach the right audience, you can choose between two targeting strategies.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.000
Keyword targeting matches your ad to relevant shopping queries.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Use broad phrase or exact match types to control reach.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Enable theme targeting to simplify setup.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Amazon's machine learning suggests relevant keywords based on shopper signals.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.000
Product targeting places your ad next to related or complementary items.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.000
This helps you reach shoppers already browsing in your category.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Choosing the right targeting method ensures your ads are relevant and timely.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.000
After launch, use campaign metrics to evaluate performance and make improvements.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.000
Track your click-through rate to see how often shoppers engage.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.037
Monitor impression share at the top of search to assess visibility and review new to brand sales

00:03:27.037 --> 00:03:30.000
to understand how many new customers your ads are reaching.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.000
These metrics help you refine your strategy and improve results over time.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:40.000
Sponsored brands give you tools to grow your presence and connect with shoppers on Amazon.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.000
To begin, log in to the Amazon Ads console and create your first sponsored brands campaign.
